FILE: app/src/fly-controls.ts
```ts
import type { FreeCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { attachConfigurableFreeControl } from "@babylonjs/lite";

// attachFreeControl binds ShiftLeft/ShiftRight to "move down" (camera-notes.md, note 55),
// so Shift would sink the camera. attachConfigurableFreeControl lets us replace the
// up/down key lists (note 16) and set a speed multiplier for the fast keys, so Shift
// only changes speed.
export function attachFlyControls(camera: FreeCamera, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, scene: SceneContext): () => void {
    return attachConfigurableFreeControl(camera, canvas, scene, {
        upKeys: ["Space"],
        downKeys: ["PageDown"],
        fastKeys: ["ShiftLeft", "ShiftRight"],
        fastMultiplier: 3,
    });
}
```

I wrote the file content above but did not save it to disk or compile it, because Babylon Lite is not installed here. The controls are built on `attachConfigurableFreeControl`, with Space and PageDown as the only vertical keys and Shift as a 3× speed key. The returned function is the library's own disposer, so I assumed it removes everything it adds.

Things I'm not sure of:
- I could not confirm that `attachConfigurableFreeControl` is exported from the package root. If it is not, the import needs a different path.
- The `.d.ts` does not say whether the configurable control keeps the default WASD/arrow move keys and the mouse-look drag. I assumed both are kept, since the notes only say `upKeys`, `downKeys` and `fastKeys` are overridden. If mouse look is missing, `attachFreeControl` is the alternative, but it would need the Shift-down problem solved another way.
- Note 16 says the library's `attachConfigurableFreeControl` replaces default up/down keys when given, which is what I rely on to keep Shift out of the vertical controls. I have not checked this against running code.
